<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 13.39 µm in Danio margaritatus (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Docstring, sweep comment, and GIF footer state k_c^2. Lean theorems state the threshold ordering, the longer successor wavelength, the 12-mode window, and that 510101 nm is 38 elementary cells with a remainder. Render thresholds are reconstruction choices and are labeled as such." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 13.39 µm in Danio margaritatus (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script integrates Schnakenberg kinetics with zero-flux boundaries, solves D_u so the linear law is exactly 1.339e-05 m, and checks that law with a periodic 1D growth series (r = 0.99999995). The nonlinear spot field's FFT peak is 17.22 µm; that shift is reported rather than overwritten. gamma = 1/s remains a chosen time unit, and the three-cell Nakamasu system is not the integrator." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 13.39 µm in Danio margaritatus (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 81/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Specimen NN median is 510.1 µm against the elementary reference 13.39 µm (they are not equal). Bootstrap 95% CI is 471–536 µm and a ±10% body-length sweep is stored. Polygon circularity is 0.708, not 1. KS D on median-scaled NN distances is 0.207. Dispersion RMSE is 5.53e-4 /s. The PCA-chord CDF Pearson is 0.977 and the odd-bin holdout is 0.770; the holdout is not rounded up to the dispersion correlation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-adult-pearl-nearest-neighbour-spacing>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-critical-wavelength-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-pearson-r-analytic-vs-1d-pde>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ks-statistic-of-median-scaled-nn-distances>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-pearl-field-circularity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-reaction-knockout-ablation-amplitude-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-cdf-pearson-versus-ellipse-marginal>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 13.39 µm in Danio margaritatus (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2. lambda_c = 13.39 µm (1.339e-05 m, log10 = -4.873) at geological age 0 Ma. Diffusion-ratio sweep is monotone and equals 13.39 µm at delta = 40. Albolineatus sigma_max = -0.0805 /s (stable). Nigrofasciatus lambda_c = 17.80 µm (unstable). Dispersion Pearson r = 0.99999995, RMSE = 5.53e-4 /s. Flank segmentation: 73 pearls, polygon circularity 0.708, aspect 1.78, median NN 510.1 µm (bootstrap 95% CI 471–536 µm). Nonlinear FFT peak of the cellular field is 17.22 µm and is plotted as a separate number. PCA-chord CDF Pearson is 0.977; odd-bin Pearson is 0.770 and is not claimed to clear 0.98. KS D on median-scaled nearest neighbours is 0.207. Reaction-knockout amplitude ratio is ~0. GIF is 720×540, 12 frames. CV similarity to the specimen is 93.3. Overall 85.9/100 (faithfulness 85.1, reproducibility 87.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 23fb4b106f961ebb8b80abe7209257c902f834ad; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 81, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/danio_margaritatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 23fb4b106f961ebb8b80abe7209257c902f834ad, image/png, 630986 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 8eac595b6d5b6eb28291aff92e3ce8801578927e4be889341429924640adbc4e (sha256 8eac595b6d5b6eb28291aff92e3ce8801578927e4be889341429924640adbc4e), spec_fingerprint b77145afbb1daaa36679993eab12015d9069adc4fe8d9a9b382f23a8172ce984. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b77145afbb1daaa36679993eab12015d9069adc4fe8d9a9b382f23a8172ce984; artifact_sha256: 8eac595b6d5b6eb28291aff92e3ce8801578927e4be889341429924640adbc4e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/danio_margaritatus_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_margaritatus_specimen.jpg=48a9005afc001e30..., datasets/danio_margaritatus_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_margaritatus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=ecf0d9be62697438...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and finite-k instability. | Nakamasu et al. 2009 pigment-cell short-range activation and long-range inhibition. | Quigley 2004, Patterson 2014, Spiewak 2018: Danio species differ in stripe and spot deployment. | Huang et al. 2021: Danio albolineatus adult coloration is not a zebrafish stripe pattern. | Conway, Chen & Mayden 2008 place the celestial pearl danio in Danio.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b, delta) for three chronospecies at this rung. | Catalog length 0.018 m on the pearl-field principal axis. | Low-pass photographic background behind the simulated hull.; transfer_boundary: 13.39 µm is sub-resolution on the adult plate (~21 µm/px). | Albolineatus and nigrofasciatus parameters are not fits to their own photographs in this slot. | gamma = 1/s sets the time unit.; does_not_claim: Adult pearl spacing is 13.39 µm. The measured median is 510.1 µm. | Odd-bin spatial Pearson exceeds 0.98. It is 0.770. | The GIF polygon is the anatomical outline. | A second assessor from another provider scored this audit.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resolved. segment_pearls requires a local blue window and drops isolated centroids. Circularity is the shoelace quotient (0.708).', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved. Sweep lambdas are 14.25, 13.87, 13.64, 13.48, 13.39, 13.34, 13.30 µm. Self-test asserts the decrease.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Resolved. Figure titles show NN 95% CI 471–536 µm and nonlinear FFT peak 17.22 µm beside linear 13.39 µm.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Resolved. Holdout uses the principal-axis chord. CDF r = 0.977, odd-bin r = 0.770, reported separately from the dispersion r.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Open. One photograph and a catalog length of 0.018 m. The ±10% length sweep moves NN from 574 to 701 µm and does not replace a measured scale bar.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': \"Open. Predecessor and successor Jacobians are reconstructions at this rung, not re-fits to those species' plates.\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': 'Open. The animated flank is the convex hull, not a traced body outline.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.59e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 13.39 µm in Danio margaritatus (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "With D_u fixed, lambda_c falls from 14.25 µm at delta = 8 to 13.30 µm at delta = 75 and is 13.39 µm at delta = 40. Albolineatus (delta 1.35) has no unstable band. Nigrofasciatus is a longer unstable wave. Reaction knockout and equal diffusion both collapse the pattern. The self-test refuses a non-monotone sweep." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
